=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: srv1
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** The Apache2 web server daemon (`apache2`) on `srv1` (IP 10.5.0.4).

**Mechanism:** The campus uses a BIND (`named`) authoritative DNS server co-located on `srv1`. The zone `jeremysitlab.com` contains a wildcard record (`* IN A 10.5.0.4`) so that every internal hostname — including `srv1.jeremysitlab.com` — resolves to 10.5.0.4. This DNS resolution is working correctly; all three office clients (pc1, pc2, pc3) successfully query `10.5.0.4:53` and receive valid answers. However, when their browsers (or curl) attempt an HTTP connection to port 80 at 10.5.0.4, there is nothing listening — apache2 is not running. The TCP connection fails immediately (curl exit code 000, 0.003 s), which browsers surface as "site can't be found," misleading the user into blaming DNS.

**Localization:** Exclusively `srv1`. The L3 fabric, OSPF routing, DNS name resolution, and all other services are healthy. Only the apache2 process on `srv1` is absent (`pgrep -a apache2` returns nothing; `ss -tlnp` shows no port 80 listener; `ps aux` shows only `bash` and `named`).

**Root cause:** The apache2 web server daemon was never started (or was stopped) on `srv1`, even though its configuration and enabled virtual-host (`/etc/apache2/sites-enabled/000-default.conf`) are fully in place.

**Fix:** Start apache2 on `srv1`: `service apache2 start` (or `apache2ctl start`). No DNS or routing changes are required.
=== END ===